---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { phases, topics, resources } from '../data/roadmap';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { ArrowUpRight } from 'lucide-react';
import Github from '../components/Github';
import { repository, url } from '../utils/urls';
const guides = await getCollection('guides');
---

<Layout title="About" active="About">
  <div class="page-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">A FIELD GUIDE, NOT A FINISH LINE</span>
    <h1>A place for people who ask why.</h1>
    <p>
      Gata Science Roadmap is an open-source learning map for data science. It connects theory to
      practice, and makes a big field feel a little more navigable.
    </p>
  </div>
  <article class="prose about-prose">
    <h2>Learn the connections, not just the tools.</h2>
    <p>
      A library can fit a model in a line of code. Understanding why it works takes a little longer.
      Gata Science Roadmap brings the mathematics back into the conversation: projections inside
      regression, probability inside classification, and the chain rule inside neural networks.
    </p>
    <h2>What’s here today</h2>
    <p>
      The first edition maps {topics.length} concepts across {phases.length} chapters, with{' '}
      {guides.length} detailed guides and {resources.length} curated resources. Every chapter has an
      explanation, prerequisites, a practice task, and sources for further study. Book icons
      identify the deeper authored lessons; other concept entries connect to their chapter
      resources. The curriculum is complete in scope, while the detailed lesson library can continue
      to grow.
    </p>
    <p>
      Progress is a personal checklist, not a certificate. Choose a path that serves your goals,
      revisit foundations when needed, and make room for projects.
    </p>
    <h2>Your learning, your browser.</h2>
    <p>
      No login, database, analytics, or paid API. Topic and project completions stay in your
      browser’s local storage. Clearing site data removes them. You can export a record from{' '}
      <a href={url('progress/')}>My Progress</a>. External resources have their own privacy
      practices.
    </p>
    <h2 id="open-source">Built in the open</h2>
    <p>
      Gata Science Roadmap is licensed under MIT. The repository includes contribution instructions,
      content schemas, issue templates, tests, and a GitHub Pages deployment workflow. Add a guide,
      improve an explanation, or share a better free resource.
    </p>
    {repository ? (
      <a class="button" href={repository}>
        <Github size={16} />
        View on GitHub
        <ArrowUpRight size={14} />
      </a>
    ) : (
      <div class="callout">
        <strong>This is a local edition.</strong>
        <p>
          The source is in this workspace. A public repository and live URL have not been configured
          yet. When a repository is connected, the GitHub links will point to it.
        </p>
      </div>
    )}
    <h2>With thanks</h2>
    <p>
      The map is inspired by the idea of interactive learning roadmaps, including roadmap.sh, with
      original design, code, and educational writing. The broader project stands on the work of
      open-source tool maintainers, documentation authors, and educators who make their materials
      freely available.
    </p>
    <p>Built with Astro, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, React Flow, KaTeX, and Lucide.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
